{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.ColorTubeFibers","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.ColorTubeFibers","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.constant_term_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.constant_term_identity","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L73-L80","doc":"The constant term of the color tube cubic is the `X = z` evaluation\nof the color cubic, written in its shifted-cubic form:\n`4z³+3z²+2z+1 = z³ + (z+1)z² + (z²+z+1)z + (z³+z²+z+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.color_tube_at_z_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.color_tube_at_z_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L66-L71","doc":"At z = 0, the color tube cubic specialises to c³ + c² + c + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.shift_isomorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.shift_isomorphism","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**Shift isomorphism**: substituting X = c + z in the color cubic yields\nthe color tube cubic. This proves the two fibres are isomorphic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colorCubicPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colorCubicPoly","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The color cubic polynomial (from color-elliptic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colorTubeCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colorTubeCubic","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L47-L51","doc":"The color tube cubic polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.cubic_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.cubic_eq","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The defining cubic relation for the color tube. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.c","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The color tube coordinate c (standing for r, g, or b). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.z","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The spacetime ratio z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorTubeFibre","kind":"structure","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L31-L45","doc":"**Color tube fibre data** at spacetime ratio z.\n\nThe affine cubic c³ + (4z+1)c² + (6z²+3z+1)c + (4z³+3z²+2z+1) = 0\ndefines the color tube R_z (equivalently G_z, B_z) at z. This is\nisomorphic to the color elliptic fibre E_z via the shift X = c + z.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §5, Color fibration ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.q_param","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.R_q","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-tube-fibers.lean#L25-L27","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}